[2026-10-18 20:35:57] render_double_emphasis(Jupiter\'s equatorial bulge is perceptible at this scale - the equatorial diameter is 6.8% larger than the polar diameter, and it is 11.25 times wider than Earth\'s.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:57] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Jupiter\'s equatorial bulge is perceptible at this scale - the equatorial diameter is 6.8% larger than the polar diameter, and it is 11.25 times wider than Earth\'s.\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:35:57] render_double_emphasis(Jupiter has lots of atmosphere! The upper deck of clouds is ammonia crystals. The lower deck is ammonium hydrogen sulfide tinted by molecules of sulfur. It is often stormy with thunder, lightening, and high winds.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:57] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Jupiter has lots of atmosphere! The upper deck of clouds is ammonia crystals. The lower deck is ammonium hydrogen sulfide tinted by molecules of sulfur. It is often stormy with thunder, lightening, and high winds.\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_header(Moon)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Earth\'s only natural satellite. The moon is 4.6 billion years old, has a mass of 7.4 X 10^(22) kg, is 2,157.6 miles (3,480 km) wide (just wide enough to fit between New York and the Rocky Mountains), and orbits the Earth at an average distance of 238,329.24 miles (384,402 km). Although the moon is much smaller than the sun, they both appear the same size in the sky because the moon is so much closer to the Earth than the sun is. When the moon appears over the horizon, we see it as much larger than it actually is. This optical illusion is called the Moon illusion.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_double_emphasis(Orbit)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Orbit\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Because of the gravitational influence of the sun, the moon\'s orbit is a slightly deformed ellipse with an eccentricity of 0.054. Since the plane of the moon\'s orbit is tilted 5\xc2\xb0 from the ecliptic (Earth-sun orbit plane), there is not a lunar and solar eclipse every month. Tidal forces have locked the moon into an orbit where it always presents the same face to Earth. It must be remembered that it is the far side and not the dark side of the moon that we cannot see; the far side of the moon is lit during new moon.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_double_emphasis(Origin)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Origin\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(The origin of the moon remains a mystery. The many theories of how the moon came to be can generally be broken down into three categories: )
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_blockcode(    1. It was broken off of the Earth.
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] 
[2026-10-18 20:35:58]     2. It is a captured body.
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] 
[2026-10-18 20:35:58]     3. It formed from the dust and gas left over when the Earth formed.
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] , (null))
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(The currently held theory of the moon\'s origin, which fits into the first of these three categories, says that an asteroid, comet, or other object slammed into the Earth and tore off vast quantities of material. This material flew into space around the Earth, and the gravitational attraction between the pieces, joined them together to form the moon. )
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_double_emphasis(Surface)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Surface\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(The moon is covered with craters and basins left by meteor impacts and maria (Latin for seas) left by lava flows from the moon\'s now dead volcanoes. The maria are the dark looking areas on the moon, such as the ones that form the \"man in the moon\". Because the moon has no atmosphere, its surface has not been eroded by weathering; however, it has been worn down slightly by micrometeor bombardment. This constant rain of tiny particles formed a layer of soil, called the regolith, on the moon.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_double_emphasis(The moon\'s terrain as seen by Apollo astronauts.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100The moon\'s terrain as seen by Apollo astronauts.\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_double_emphasis(How we thought it would look. The moon is much smoother than we used to think, based on its appearance in a telescope.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100How we thought it would look. The moon is much smoother than we used to think, based on its appearance in a telescope.\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_double_emphasis(If you lived on a part of the moon where the Earth was visible in the sky, it would float in that one spot forever, never rising or setting.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100If you lived on a part of the moon where the Earth was visible in the sky, it would float in that one spot forever, never rising or setting.\x01\x0e-0100)
