[2026-10-18 20:35:58] 
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] , 3)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_header(Coma Berenices)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_double_emphasis(Coma Berenices (Berenice)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_double_emphasis(s Hair))
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Coma Berenices (Berenice\x01\x0e-0100\'\x01\x0e+0100s Hair)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Small dim constellation located under the handle of the Big Dipper and containing a multitude of galaxies. Coma Berenices was said to be the gift of Queen Berenice of Egypt, who cut her hair and gave it to the gods in thanks for the return of her husband.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_header(Comet)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Small body that orbits the sun. Comets\' volatile material in their nuclei and their eccentric (elongated) orbit separate them from asteroids. Despite being made of ice, the nucleus of a comet, which is the most permanent feature, is very flimsy. As comets approach the sun, its radiation converts some of their volatile material into a fuzzy tail (the word comet comes from the Greek word for \"hairy one\"). This tail is pushed away from the sun by the solar wind. The average length of the tail is 62 million miles (100 million km), and the average size of the nucleus is 6.2 miles (10 km). The albedo of a comet (2% to 4%) is one of the lowest of any object in our solar system.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph( Comets are named by the year and order in which they were discovered (e.g., 1990a, 1990b). Later, they are renamed according to when they reached perihelion (e.g., 1990I, 1990II).)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Comets can be divided by their period of orbit into either short (less than 20 years), intermediate (between 20 and 200 years), and long (more than 200 years) term comets. In this system of division, Halley\'s comet would have an intermediate term.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Because people of ancient times believed that the heavens were perfect and stable, the appearance of a comet was taken as an omen of famine and death. It was not until the 1500\'s when Tycho Brahe determined that comets were within the solar system, that people began to believe that comets were celestial objects.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(The present model of comets, presented by Fred Whipple in 1950, is often called the \"dirty snowball\" model. This model states that comets are made mainly of ice, with some dust particles trapped inside. As the comet approaches the sun, some of the dust particles are released as the comet\'s fuzzy tail. Consequently, after the comet orbits the sun enough times, all its material will be released.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Comets come from the Oort cloud, a cloud of material roughly 40,000 to 50,000 a.u. away. The existence of the Oort cloud was suggested by Jan Hendrick Oort and confirmed by Brian G. Marsden. The Oort cloud is thought to have formed out of the accretion disk that also made the planets.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_header(Command Module)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Christened during the Apollo program, the command module housed the crew as they journeyed into space and remained orbiting the moon while two crew members went to the surface in the lunar module.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_header(Communications Satellites)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Orbiting devices that allow for communication around the world without bulky fibers and cables. For communication to take place, microwave signals are sent from one location, bounced off a satellite, and sent to another location. The microwave signals that carry messages to and from communications satellites are called carrier waves. Each carrier wave can carry hundreds of messages, and carrier waves can be sent in many different frequencies. Because one communications satellite cannot cover more than about a third of the world, approximately three satellites are needed to cover the whole world.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_header(Conjunction)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_list_start((null), 1)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(Two planets that seem to approach each other from our Earthly perspective.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_listitem(Two planets that seem to approach each other from our Earthly perspective.
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] 
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] , 3)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_emphasis(Inferior conjunction)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_emphasis(Superior conjunction)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_paragraph(A line-up in space: a)\x01\x0e+0200Inferior conjunction\x01\x0e-0200 when a planet lines up with the Earth and the sun so that it is in between the Earth and the sun and b)\x01\x0e+0200Superior conjunction\x01\x0e-0200 when the planet lines up with the Earth and the sun so that the sun is between the planet and the Earth.)
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] render_listitem(A line-up in space: a)\x01\x0e+0200Inferior conjunction\x01\x0e-0200 when a planet lines up with the Earth and the sun so that it is in between the Earth and the sun and b)\x01\x0e+0200Superior conjunction\x01\x0e-0200 when the planet lines up with the Earth and the sun so that the sun is between the planet and the Earth.
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] 
[2026-10-18 20:35:58] , 3)
