[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_double_emphasis(Mars Facts:)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Mars Facts:\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Average Daytime Temperature is about 22 F (-5 C))
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Pressure is about 0.006 Earth atmospheres)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mass)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Measure of how much matter a body contains. The more matter a body contains, the more inertia it has. (Inertia is how much the object either wants to stay where it is or keep moving in the same direction at the same speed.)  For example, a bowling ball has more mass than a baseball does, so it is easier to move the baseball than it is to move the bowling ball. Note: Mass is not the same as weight. If we moved the bowling ball and baseball into outer space, both would weigh nothing, but the bowling ball would still be harder to move than the baseball.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mass-Luminosity Ratio)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(General trend for more massive stars to have a greater absolute brightness.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mauna Kea Observatory)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Located on an extinct volcano in Hawaii and considered to be on the best observing spot in the world. It now contains the Keck telescope, the largest reflecting telescope in the world.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mcmath Telescope)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_double_emphasis(McMath Telescope)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100McMath Telescope\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Solar telescope on top of Kitt Peak Mountain in Arizona. It is the world\'s largest solar observatory and has an aperture of 44 inches (152 cm).)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mensa)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_double_emphasis(Mensa (The Table Mountain))
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Mensa (The Table Mountain)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Dim southern constellation that includes part of the Large Magellanic Cloud.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mercury)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(First planet from the sun. Mercury is odd in many ways, more resembling the moon than any other planet. It has a small radius (1,043 miles, 1,738 km), but it has a large, solid iron core and a density 5.45 times that of water. In order to escape Mercury\'s gravity, you must travel 2.6 miles (4.3 km) per second. Its rather eccentric orbit is tilted 7\xc2\xb0 off the plane of the ecliptic. Much to the surprise of astronomers, Mercury has a magnetic field and a weak atmosphere that is composed chiefly of sodium and potassium.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(It was once believed that the same side of Mercury always faced the sun, but it was discovered that it actually rotates on its axis every 58.64 days. This figure is exactly two-thirds of its 87.97 day orbit, meaning Mercury spins on its axis three times for every two orbits it makes. )
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_double_emphasis(Visibility)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Visibility\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Mercury is notoriously hard to see. This is because it is visible for only a few weeks every year and because it never rises more than 28\xc2\xb0 above the horizon while the sun is below the horizon. Although it is bright due to its proximity to the sun, it is not possible to make out any surface features from the Earth. Mariner 10 visited Mercury and discovered that it is covered with impact craters, including a 850 mile (1,400 km) wide impact crater later named the Caloris Basin. Opposite this basin there is an interesting terrain of dissected hills, large valleys, disfigured craters, and great landslides. Another interesting feature on Mercury is that it has polar ice caps.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_double_emphasis(Mercury Facts:)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Mercury Facts:\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Daytime Temperature is about 826 F (427 C))
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Because Mercury has no measurable atmosphere of light gases, it has no measurable atmospheric pressure. This means that Mercury has no oxygen, nitrogen, carbon dioxide, or water vapor.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mercury Project)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(First American space program that was the first to put an American man into space and return him safely to Earth.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Meridian)
