[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mimas)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Second satellite from Saturn, with a diameter of 300 miles (500 km). Mimas has a crater 242 miles (390 km) across, giving it the appearance of an eyeball. At a distance of 115,320 miles (184,512 km) from Saturn, Mimas orbits it in 22 hours and 37 minutes.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mintaka)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Along with Betelgeuse and Zeta Orionis, makes up Orion\'s belt. Mintaka is the western most star in the belt. Mintaka is a double star with a magnitude of 2.2, and lies about 1,500 lighters away.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mir)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Current Soviet space station in orbit since 1986. Cosmonauts, while housed in the Mir station, has shattered duration records. In 1988, two cosmonauts remained in orbit for 366 days.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_double_emphasis(The Mir Space Lab is still up there.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100The Mir Space Lab is still up there.\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mir)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(Current Soviet space station in orbit since 1986. Cosmonauts, while housed in the Mir station, has shattered duration records. In 1988, two cosmonauts remained in orbit for 366 days.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_double_emphasis(The Mir Space Lab is still up there.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100The Mir Space Lab is still up there.\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:00] render_header(Mir)
