[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Triangulum)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Triangulum (The Triangle))
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Triangulum (The Triangle)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Small northern constellation between Andromeda and Perseus. Although it has been identified since ancient times, it contains no bright stars. It does hold the spiral galaxy M33, a member of the Local Group that is about 2.3 million light years away.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Triangulum Australe)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Triangulum Australe (The Southern Triangle))
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Triangulum Australe (The Southern Triangle)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Small but distinctive southern constellation that lies on the edge of the band of stars called the Milky Way. The brightest star shines at magnitude 1.88 and is 99 lightyears distant. The second brightest star is 39 lightyears away and twinkles at magnitude 3.04. The third brightest star completes the triangle and glimmers at magnitude 3.06.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Trifid Nebula)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Trifid Nebula (M20))
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Trifid Nebula (M20)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Cloud of ionized gas in Sagittarius that gets its name from the dust lanes that cross it and divide it into three parts.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Triple Star System)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Group of three stars that orbit a common center of mass.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Triton)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Triton)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Triton\x01\x0e-0100 )
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Neptune\'s largest moon. It measures 1,700 miles (2,735 km) and has a retrograde (westward) orbit. One theory says that Triton\'s weird orbit resulted from a near collision with another Neptunian moon, which escaped to become the planet Pluto. Triton\'s -400\xc2\xb0 F (-240\xc2\xb0 C) surface temperature might make it the coldest object in our solar system. Triton\'s surface is covered with ice that is speckled with craters. Its surface is re-coated with ice when gases escape from its interior during its summer and go right from gas to ice when exposed to the cold temperatures.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Triton Facts:)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Triton Facts:\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Temperature:    37.5\xc2\xb0 K)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Pressure:    10 millionths of the Earth\'s atmosphere)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Atmosphere:    mainly nitrogen)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Ten percent of Triton\'s surface is composed of solid carbon dioxide, however, it has little carbon dioxide in its atmosphere and may have solid ice beneath its surface but no water vapor or oxygen.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Trojans)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Two groups of asteroids that share Jupiter\'s orbit. If lines are drawn in to connect these two groups of asteroids with Jupiter, an equilateral triangle will be formed. However, because these asteroids are perturbed by other planets, they wander away from their usual points, L4 and L5. The first Trojan asteroid discovered was 588 Achilles in 1906, but a recent survey suggests that there are as many as 700 asteroids brighter than magnitude 21 orbit near points L4 and L5.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Tsiolkovsky, Konstantin Eduardovich)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Tsiolkovsky, Konstantin Eduardovich (1857-1935))
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Tsiolkovsky, Konstantin Eduardovich (1857-1935)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Brilliant pioneer of early rocketry who is often called the Father of Astronautics. Although he was a teacher by profession, he drew and designed plans for a gas-filled metal dirigible (an aircraft that is lighter than air) and built the first Russian wind tunnel. He studied aerodynamics and outlined principles of flight long before the Wright brothers built their airplane. His earliest article on spaceflight, \"Free Space\" (1883), described the true weightless conditions of orbit.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(By 1898, he had devised a theory of rocket propulsion by finding how the rocket\'s final speed relates to its exhaust velocity, which is how fast the gas escapes from the back of the rocket. He also devised equations showing how the amount of fuel a rocket needs relates to its weight. In 1903, he published \"Exploration of Space by Reactive Devices,\" which describes how space rockets could burn liquid hydrogen and liquid oxygen, a principle still used in modern spacecrafts. Tsiolkovsky also drew plans for multi-stage rockets when he realized that single-stage rockets were not powerful enough to escape Earth\'s gravity.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(T Tauri Stars)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(A type of very young star in an early phase of its life where contraction is still taking place. T-Tauris (star T in the constellation Taurus), named after the first of its kind to be recognized, are stars that have not yet started fusion but glow in infrared and heat the clouds of gas and dust that surround them. As they contract, they heat up and sweep away their encircling shell of gas. Astronomers have proposed that these stars do not change their light output, but they appear to vary because the material swirling around them eclipses their light. Large numbers of T-Tauri stars have been discovered through the strong infrared radiation that they emit. Loose groupings of T-Tauri stars are known as T associations.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Tucana)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Tucana (The Toucan))
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Tucana (The Toucan)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Constellation near the celestial south pole that contains the Smaller Magellanic Cloud. Tucana also has a bright globular cluster, 47 Tucanae (NGC 104), which shines at magnitude 3 and is about 19,000 light years away. The second brightest star of Tucana is a complex multiple-star system.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Tunguska or Tunguska Event)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Site of an explosion in Siberia on June 30, 1908. Witnesses reported seeing a fireball as bright as the sun streaking across the sky and then hearing a deafening explosion. Although scientists estimate that the blast occurred 5 miles (8 km) above the Earth, it snapped trees in a 20-25 mile (30-40 km) radius. No humans died because the region was an un-populated wilderness. The cause of this explosion has puzzled scientists. Since it did not carve a crater, some speculate a comet or meteor exploded in the atmosphere.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Twilight)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(The time before sunrise or after sunset when the sun is below the horizon. Twilight is classified according to how far below the horizon the sun has dropped. The three types are Civil twilight (sun is about 6 below the horizon), Nautical twilight (sun is about 12 below the horizon), and Astronomical twilight (sun is about 18 below the horizon).)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Crepuscular rays: the pink glow on atmospheric dust or water vapor is interrupted by the shadows of distant cumulus clouds that tower thousands of feet into the air, producing these familiar streaks at twilight.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Crepuscular rays: the pink glow on atmospheric dust or water vapor is interrupted by the shadows of distant cumulus clouds that tower thousands of feet into the air, producing these familiar streaks at twilight.\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Twilight)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(The time before sunrise or after sunset when the sun is below the horizon. Twilight is classified according to how far below the horizon the sun has dropped. The three types are Civil twilight (sun is about 6 below the horizon), Nautical twilight (sun is about 12 below the horizon), and Astronomical twilight (sun is about 18 below the horizon).)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_double_emphasis(Crepuscular rays: the pink glow on atmospheric dust or water vapor is interrupted by the shadows of distant cumulus clouds that tower thousands of feet into the air, producing these familiar streaks at twilight.)
