[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Tycho)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_emphasis(See Brahe, Tycho.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0200See Brahe, Tycho.\x01\x0e-0200)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(UFO)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Unidentified Flying Objects. Although UFOs are often reported by the public and even trained observers, at least 99% of these sightings turn out to be aircraft, bright stars or planets, meteors, satellites, etc. However, so far, the rest of the sightings have gone unexplained. Astronomers do not believe UFOs are extraterrestrial visitors, and few astronomers have ever claimed to see one.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Ultraviolet Astronomy)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Study of the universe\'s objects that radiate primarily in ultraviolet energy, which lies between visible light and x-rays and has a wavelength between 3000 and 300 angstroms (1 angstrom = 1 ten-billionth of a meter). Such investigations reveal violent activity because a body must be heated above 50,000 degrees to radiate mostly ultraviolet. Using ultraviolet astronomy, it is possible to understand some of the dynamic processes in the lives and evolution of stars and galaxies, as well as identify which elements are present in interstellar space and to examine the atmospheres of stars and planets. Only space satellites can observe ultraviolet sources because most of the rays do not penetrate Earth\'s atmosphere.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_header(Umbra)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_list_start((null), 1)
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_paragraph(Darkest part of a shadow. People in the strip of the Earth in the moon\'s umbra during a solar eclipse see a total eclipse, while the part of the Earth in the moon\'s penumbra (partial shadow) sees a partial eclipse. )
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] render_listitem(Darkest part of a shadow. People in the strip of the Earth in the moon\'s umbra during a solar eclipse see a total eclipse, while the part of the Earth in the moon\'s penumbra (partial shadow) sees a partial eclipse. 
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] 
[2026-10-18 20:36:01] , 3)
