[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_header(Whirlpool Galaxy)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_double_emphasis(Whirlpool Galaxy (M51))
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100Whirlpool Galaxy (M51)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(Beautiful spiral galaxy viewed face-own in the constellation Canes Venatici. The Whirlpool galaxy lies only 13 million lightyears away and is a magnificent sight in backyard telescopes.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_double_emphasis(M51, the Whirlpool galaxy, is a spiral just under the end of the Big Dipper\'s handle. The smaller galaxy, NGC 5195, has brushed past M51, disrupting the spiral arms in the process.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100M51, the Whirlpool galaxy, is a spiral just under the end of the Big Dipper\'s handle. The smaller galaxy, NGC 5195, has brushed past M51, disrupting the spiral arms in the process.\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_header(White Dwarf)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(Dying stars whose diameters are 1/100 that of the sun (about equal to Earth\'s), whose luminosities are 1/10,000 that of the sun, and whose masses are less than the Chandrasekhar limit (1.4 times that of the sun). The resulting densities of a white dwarf are 1,000,000 times that of water.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(Although usually white, white dwarfs can be any color. Their color is dictated by their surface temperature, and the hottest white dwarfs, which were the first to be discovered, were white. The white dwarf stage is the second to last stage in the death of a star whose final mass (after its outer layers have been shed) is less than 1.4 times that of the sun. After these stars fuse all their hydrogen, they start to collapse. When, due to the collapse, they have a high enough temperature to begin fusing again, the fusion starts with a jump, and they expand into a red giant.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(After the red giant loses most of its mass to solar wind, it becomes a planetary nebula and loses more mass to solar wind. The cooled nucleus of the planetary nebula is the white dwarf. These dying stars are no longer producing energy from fusion, and their light comes from the escape of their internal heat. When they lose this heat, they will lose their brightness and become black dwarfs. Since they are no longer fusing, there is no energy to counter the crushing effects of gravity, and they are in a state of collapse. Consequently, their matter is degenerate, which means that electrons have escaped from their atoms and are packed tightly together. The force stopping white dwarfs from collapsing into neutron stars or black holes is degeneracy, which comes from electrons\' resistance to each other.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(When calculations are carried out to determine what dimensions white dwarfs must have in order to be stable, it is found that the more mass a white dwarf has, the smaller it will be. The most famous white dwarf is Sirius B, companion to Sirius.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_header(White, Edward Higgins II)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_double_emphasis(White, Edward Higgins II (1930-1967))
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100White, Edward Higgins II (1930-1967)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(On June 3, 1965, became the first American to walk in space. During his 21 minute walk outside Gemini 4, he moved about with the aid of a hand-held gas gun. White was killed during a fire when he was training for an Apollo mission.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_header(White Sands Proving Ground)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_double_emphasis(White Sands Proving Ground (White Sands Missile Range))
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100White Sands Proving Ground (White Sands Missile Range)\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(US Army testing range in White Sands, New Mexico that was first used in 1945 to test the American Wac Corporal sounding rocket. Werner Von Braun later used White Sands to launch captured V-2 rockets. This area is still used to test missiles and warheads.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_header(Wolf-Rayet Stars)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(Members of a class of rare (only about 200 identified), exceptionally hot stars with surface temperatures of at least 30,000\xc2\xb0 K, but with an unusual surface composition richer in helium, carbon, and nitrogen than most stars. Although their place in the aging process of a star is not fully understood, astronomers believe they lie inside a rapidly expanding envelope of gas. Wolf-Rayet stars are believed to be stars that began with a very high mass, but eventually blew away most of their outer layers of gas exposing their cores in which helium and heavier elements have accumulated due to hydrogen fusion. The ejected gas shells sometimes make a visible nebula around the star.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_header(X-Ray Astronomy)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_double_emphasis(X-ray Astronomy)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(\x01\x0e+0100X-ray Astronomy\x01\x0e-0100)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(Study of space using electromagnetic radiation with wavelengths from 0.1 to 300 angstroms (X-rays). On June 18, 1962, X-ray astronomy began with the launch of the Aerobee sounding rocket. It was expected that this rocket would find X-rays coming from the sun\'s radiation hitting the moon\'s surface, but none were found. Instead, strong X-rays were found coming from the direction of Scorpius, and slight X-rays were found coming from all directions. Many satellites with devices for detecting X-rays were launched in the 1970\'s, with ANS-1, Ariel V, Copernicus, and Uhuru among them. The sun\'s X-rays, which arise mainly from the corona\'s hot gas, have also been studied by, among other devices, the Orbiting Solar Observatory (OSO). )
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(There are several known X-ray producers:)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_list_start(, 1)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(Black holes are thought to be detectable through X-ray astronomy. It has been determined that the star Cygnus X-1 is a double star system, and the calculated mass of one of the companions makes it a good black hole candidate. X-rays coming from Cygnus X-1 may be emitted when material falls into the black hole by whirling around in an accretion disk before reaching the event horizon. Alternatively, Cygnus X-1 may be a triple star system. If the large unseen companion\'s mass was divided between two stars, neither would be a black hole.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_listitem(Black holes are thought to be detectable through X-ray astronomy. It has been determined that the star Cygnus X-1 is a double star system, and the calculated mass of one of the companions makes it a good black hole candidate. X-rays coming from Cygnus X-1 may be emitted when material falls into the black hole by whirling around in an accretion disk before reaching the event horizon. Alternatively, Cygnus X-1 may be a triple star system. If the large unseen companion\'s mass was divided between two stars, neither would be a black hole.
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] 
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] , 3)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(The Crab Nebula, which was created in a 1054 AD supernova, is a strong emitter of X-rays, which are thought to be produced by the interactions of the speeding electrons of the pulsar at the center, and the magnetic field.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_listitem(The Crab Nebula, which was created in a 1054 AD supernova, is a strong emitter of X-rays, which are thought to be produced by the interactions of the speeding electrons of the pulsar at the center, and the magnetic field.
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] 
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] , 3)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(Extragalactic X-ray sources, such as Magellanic clouds, quasars, radio and Seyfert galaxies, and the area between galaxies that are at the center of galactic clusters. )
