[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_paragraph(Scorpius X-1: Sco X-1, the first X-ray source discovered. Sco X-1 shows strong ultraviolet emission that sometimes jumps to greater intensity. Sco X-1\'s steady X-ray emission is about 100,000 times the sun\'s total luminosity. Because it generates so much energy and because its ultraviolet emission sometimes flares, Sco X-1 is thought to be a double star system, one of whose stars is a neutron star. The emission flares are thought to come from the material that gets pulled onto the neutron star from its companion. As this material heads toward the neutron star, it rotates, forming an accretion disk. As the material rotates and falls, it heats up, reaching millions of degrees Kelvin, and emits x-ray\'s and other wavelengths.)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_list_start(, 1)
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] render_listitem(X-ray binaries are double star systems where the denser of the two stars can be detected only by its X-ray emission.
[2026-10-18 20:36:02] , 1)
